Open Codex with a model

Usage: wally codex [OPTIONS] [args...]

Arguments:
  args                        Passed through to codex

Options:
  -h, --help                  Show help
  -m, --model TEXT            A model on this machine, or a hosted one from your
                              account
      --context-window INT    Tell Codex the model holds this many tokens, so it
                              compacts sooner
      --serve                 Print the endpoint and keep it open instead of
                              launching

Examples:
  # The certified local coding model
  wally codex -m qwen3-4b-instruct-2507

  # A hosted model (needs `wally account login`)
  wally codex -m glm-5.3-flash

  # Pass arguments through to Codex after --
  wally codex -m glm-5.3-flash -- exec "explain this project"
